1. SSD (Single Shot Detector)

In your Face Mask Detection project, SSD is used for Face Detection.

What does SSD do?

When the webcam captures an image:

Camera Frame
      ↓
SSD Face Detector
      ↓
Find Faces
      ↓
Draw Face Coordinates

Example:

+-------------------+
|                   |
|      😀 Face      |
|                   |
+-------------------+

SSD finds:

startX = 100
startY = 50
endX   = 200
endY   = 180

These coordinates tell where the face is located.

Why SSD?
Fast detection
Real-time performance
Good accuracy
Works well with webcam video

In your code:

faceNet = cv2.dnn.readNet(
    "deploy.prototxt",
    "res10_300x300_ssd_iter_140000.caffemodel"
)

This is the OpenCV DNN SSD Face Detector.

2. ROI (Region of Interest)

ROI means:

Region of Interest

After SSD detects the face, we don't need the whole image.

We only need the face portion.

Example

Original Frame:

+--------------------------+
| Wall     😀 Face         |
| Chair                 Fan|
+--------------------------+

SSD detects face.

ROI extracts only:

+-----------+
|   😀 Face |
+-----------+

Everything else is removed.

Flow
Web Camera
      ↓
Full Frame
      ↓
SSD Face Detection
      ↓
Face Coordinates
      ↓
ROI Extraction
      ↓
Face Image Only
      ↓
Resize 224×224
      ↓
MobileNetV2
      ↓
Mask Prediction

================

SSD (Single Shot Detector):
A deep learning object detection algorithm used to detect faces in real-time video frames.

ROI (Region of Interest):
The cropped face area extracted from the detected image and given to MobileNetV2 for mask classification.

One-Line Viva Answer

SSD detects the face, and ROI extracts only the detected face region for mask prediction. 

